      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This problem occurs when the parent object is initially hidden in Local and its child objects need to be synchronized.\nBecause of Local, the player who comes later repeats the error internally without being able to refer to the child object because the parent object is not active.\nThe solution is to not hide the parent object in Local.\nIf necessary to improve FPS,\nHide the parent object immediately as PlayerLocal at the spawn point. By doing so, you can reference child objects.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
